# Release and Improvement Evidence

> The Awtsmoos renews the frame, the test, the branch, and the door through which the living change may flow;  
> Awtsmoos.com binds speed to truth, and truth to release, so deployed vessels reveal what measurements know.

## Render Improvement

The cinematic pixel core was profiled rather than parallelized blindly. `PixelCanvas.js` was fully rewritten to cache decoded colors and use direct bounded RGB writes inside filled primitives.

Measured representative-frame result:

- baseline mean: 2020.09 ms/frame;
- optimized mean: about 193.4 ms/frame;
- mean speedup: about 10.45x;
- baseline median: 1485.51 ms/frame;
- optimized median: about 182.58 ms/frame;
- median speedup: about 8.14x;
- seven canonical cinematic frame SHA-256 hashes remained byte-identical.

A sustained 120-frame 12 FPS sample measured about 141.94 ms/frame, roughly 7.05 freshly rendered frames/second. That evidence rejected a child-process frame farm as unnecessary complexity for this pass.

The original 12 FPS exporter subsequently rendered the complete 180-second acceptance movie successfully:

- 2,160 freshly rendered frames;
- 180 seconds;
- 640x360;
- H.264 video with AAC audio;
- approximately 4.31 minutes exporter wall time.

## AI Improvement

The deterministic fallback previously forced essentially the same busy semantic layer recipe into every prompt. It now uses feature policy, camera grammar, and semantic layer composition so requested restraint is real as well as requested richness.

Focused acceptance passed 5/5:

- 2D-only motion graphics remain 2D and omit unwanted spatial/chart/particle/character layers;
- infographics create chart/label/graphic semantics without forced 3D noise;
- tutorials create presenter, step, callout, and text semantics;
- 3D product demos create spatial/model/particle semantics and honor explicit orbit intent;
- hybrid character stories deliberately combine requested 2D and 3D semantics with camera variety.

## Release Hardening

The repository had a mixed working tree and upstream movement. A previous merge attempt appeared resolved but still contained raw conflict markers in 22 files. The release gate rejected that state before publication. The poisoned overlap was repaired and source/build contracts were reverified.

Additional unrelated release regressions found and closed during this gate:

- MitzvahWorld production/source parity repaired and verified 9/9;
- homepage direct release routes restored for Torah Library, Social Hub, Tunnel Control, and Code;
- home-source verification passed;
- a stale comments white-box policy test was replaced by a real modular runtime contract;
- comments suite passed 18/18 after the repair.

## Repository-Wide Evidence

The broad root `npm test` completed with exit code 0 after about 224.5 seconds. It included route coverage, Treasury, CSS ownership/quality, Heichelos quality, profile menu, governance, post submissions, comments, API keys, graph, social content, notifications, packed migration/repair, packed engine, platform operations/execution, Node client syntax, and Dayuh cutover.

Previously banked focused suites also include:

- Awtsmoos Studio: 5/5;
- shared movie: 27/27;
- MitzvahWorld: 9/9;
- AI semantic richness: 5/5;
- PixelCanvas regression: canonical cinematic hashes preserved;
- repository hygiene: clean over roughly 46.9k tracked files / 359 MiB;
- staged conflict-marker, diff-integrity, and explicit secret-pattern gates: clean on the earlier release snapshot.

## Deployment Rule

The repository GitHub Actions file is not a valid deployment authority in the inspected state. Production authority is the guarded `scripts/bhRelease.mjs` path, which must deploy an exact pushed SHA and verify production/public access.

No release is called deployed until local HEAD, remote `main`, activation SHA, and production verification are all observed to agree.

## Current Release Boundary

Root tests are green, but concurrent agents landed additional Studio federation/backend/export and Apps-filter changes after that root run began. Those changes must be collected into the final snapshot and receive their own focused validation before commit/push/activation.

## Post-Deploy Improvement Frontier

After the exact current snapshot is pushed and verified in production, continue with:

- Studio semantic-richness and target-fidelity UX;
- render-quality/profile controls that do not alter canonical movie content;
- real-3D renderer convergence and capability truthfulness;
- desktop/mobile browser interaction and overflow/accessibility proof;
- further duplication and technical-debt discovery across Studio adapters and shared libraries.
